<!--
  RM_MirrorGiant.xml                     RimMandrake — COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1

  Resolves ledger slug
  `dune_sea+deep_desert:mirror-plated-sun-axis-asymmetric-giant`
  (dune_sea.md SS4: "every organism is polarised on the sun-axis... the
  sun-face is mirror, ceramic, ablative armour... the shade-face carries
  every opening the organism has"; SS4's own "Roster consequences" names
  "mirror/ceramic-plated surface megafauna" and "sun-axis-asymmetric
  bodies" as WANTED). roster's own new_defs entry (rosters/
  dune_sea_deep_desert.json): "mirror-plated sun-axis asymmetric giant",
  mechanic_load "none blocking" — a pure def/art commission, no C# owed
  for the giant itself.

  Design record: EXTREME_DESERT_GIANT_COMMENSALS_1 (closed) raised this
  exact creature as an open question — "an existing RUT_ExtremeDesert
  giant (reskin/verify) or a new mirror-plated chassis authored to the
  letter of SS4's sun-face/shade-face split?" — and left it undecided.
  Resolved here as a NEW chassis: none of the biome's three existing
  giants (RSW_KraytDragon/RSW_GreaterKraytDragon/RSW_WarWyrm, all cast in
  cast_assignment.csv to a DIFFERENT ecological read — "subsurface
  strike"/"the giant" as ambush/bulk, never "surface-walking moving
  shadow") carry the sun-face/shade-face asymmetry this slug asks for, and
  that asymmetry is a property of the ART (a genuinely two-toned body,
  mirror-bright dorsal / soft-and-dark ventral), not something a uniform
  retint of an existing texture can express — so this is authored as a
  new invented (non-canon) chassis rather than a reskin, and correctly
  lives RM_-tier per Q11a (an invented name is not Star Wars IP) rather
  than routed through the RSW_/Utinni patch layer.

  Body: plain vanilla QuadrupedAnimalWithHooves (Elephant/Muffalo family)
  at giant scale — "a hundred-tonne walker" (SS4) reads as slow, massive,
  four-legged megafauna, no new BodyDef needed and no Star Wars body
  dependency for an RM_-tier def. Herbivore/grazer, non-aggressive: SS4's
  giants are described as load-bearing terrain features and shade-casters
  for the ecology living in them, not predators — trainability None (same
  "indifferent to the intelligent races" law this mod family already uses
  for other extreme-biome giants).

  Per RUT_ExtremeDesert.xml's own 2026-09-24 freeze banner ("every CONTENT
  fix for the Extreme Desert lands in mandrake.rm.stillsand only, never
  here"), this new species is authored directly in RM_Stillsand and wired
  into RM_Stillsand_Biome.xml's own (until now empty) wildAnimals node —
  not patched onto the frozen RUT_ twin, and not routed through
  WildAnimals_Stillsand.xml (that file exists only to replay
  ALREADY-EXISTING Star-Wars-named content copied off the frozen twin; a
  brand new RM_-tier def owned by this mod needs no patch at all). The
  live world (still running on frozen RUT_ExtremeDesert.xml until Phase
  B's repaint) does not carry this giant yet, by design — same posture
  wave 11's RUT_YearningFruit used for RUT_Greentide.

  Commonality set below every existing giant's own (WarWyrm 0.2,
  KraytDragon 0.15, GreaterKraytDragon 0.001) per dune_sea.md's own
  "Population target: sparse to the point of discomfort... a correct dune
  sea map is mostly nothing."

  Art: no existing render found for "mirror giant"/"sun-axis giant"/
  "mirrorplated" in infrastructure/artpipe/{done,pending,registry.jsonl}
  (checked this pass). One 3-facing job filed, rmmirrorgiant_v1_{south,
  east,north} — prompt written to require the sun-face/shade-face split
  explicitly (mirror-white, hard-edged dorsal plating vs. dark, soft
  ventral/shaded flank), the one property a reskin could never carry.

  🔴 THE NAME IS NOT SETTLED — RM_MirrorGiant is the INTERNAL working
  defName (same posture RUT_SealedSleeper/RUT_MortuaryCrawler used). No
  Stillsand shipping-names card exists yet; filed
  STILLSAND_SHIPPING_NAMES_1 this pass to cover it.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_MirrorGiant</defName>
    <label>mirror giant</label>
    <description>A walking mountain whose upper hide is a fused sheet of mirror-bright, ablative plate — nothing soft is ever turned toward the sun. Every opening it has, every soft fold of skin, every sense organ, lives instead on its lower, shaded flank, permanently turned away from the light. It moves at the pace of a shadow on a sundial, and the shade it throws is the coolest, busiest ground for a hundred kilometres in any direction. Nothing here has ever needed to chase anything; the giant simply keeps walking, and whatever needs shade learns to walk with it.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>1.8</MoveSpeed>
      <Mass>90000</Mass>
      <MarketValue>4200</MarketValue>
      <Wildness>0.9</Wildness>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-20</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>999</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>1.6</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1.2</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>3.5</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <PainShockThreshold>1.0</PainShockThreshold>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>plated foreleg</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>30</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.6</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontLeftLeg</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>plated foreleg</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>30</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.6</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontRightLeg</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>QuadrupedAnimalWithHooves</body>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <baseBodySize>18.0</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>20.0</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.4</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>VegetarianRoughAnimal</foodType>
      <leatherDef>Leather_Heavy</leatherDef>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <wildness>0.9</wildness>
      <roamMtbDays>40</roamMtbDays>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0.02</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <lifeExpectancy>400</lifeExpectancy>
      <gestationPeriodDays>90</gestationPeriodDays>
      <litterSizeCurve>
        <points>
          <li>(0.5, 0)</li>
          <li>(1, 1)</li>
          <li>(1.5, 0)</li>
        </points>
      </litterSizeCurve>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>2</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>5</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
      <soundEating>Muffalo_Eat</soundEating>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalExotic</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
